WEBVTT

﻿1
00:01:30.049 --> 00:01:33.134
What the hell do you think
you're doing, Private?

2
00:01:33.135 --> 00:01:34.761
- Private Park Yun--
- Private!

3
00:01:34.762 --> 00:01:36.638
- Speak up, Private!
- Private!

4
00:01:36.639 --> 00:01:38.973
- Private!
- Private Park Yun-seung.

5
00:01:38.974 --> 00:01:40.684
Rookie. Are you nervous?

6
00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.395
Do you see that guy
who's about to go home?

7
00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:47.023
He was stuck here for a year and a half,

8
00:01:47.024 --> 00:01:48.483
and he's going home at last.

9
00:01:48.484 --> 00:01:49.819
Are you jealous?

10
00:01:50.236 --> 00:01:52.487
- No, sir.
- Come on. Be honest.

11
00:01:52.488 --> 00:01:54.198
Yes, sir. I'm jealous, sir.

12
00:01:55.533 --> 00:01:57.493
I'm jealous too, damn it.

13
00:01:58.369 --> 00:01:59.702
I feel bad for you.

14
00:01:59.703 --> 00:02:03.958
You will never get to experience
being discharged from the army.

15
00:02:04.458 --> 00:02:06.418
Because the world will end
before that happens.

16
00:02:08.712 --> 00:02:10.798
Isn't that right, Sergeant Lee Jae-yoon?

17
00:02:11.632 --> 00:02:12.591
Darn it!

18
00:02:13.217 --> 00:02:15.344
I saw that civilian smile.

19
00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:17.763
I'm so fucking jealous.

20
00:02:20.349 --> 00:02:21.642
<i>Salute!</i>

21
00:02:22.476 --> 00:02:23.352
Salute.

22
00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.521
As of today, June 18, 2026,

23
00:02:26.522 --> 00:02:31.694
I, Sergeant Lee Jae-yoon,
am officially discharged from duty!

24
00:02:32.361 --> 00:02:33.987
Salute!

25
00:02:33.988 --> 00:02:35.155
Salute.

26
00:02:36.073 --> 00:02:38.157
- You did well, Jae-yoon.
- Thank you, sir!

27
00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:39.659
Best of luck in your future endeavors.

28
00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:40.703
Thank you, sir!

29
00:02:41.078 --> 00:02:41.954
Goodbye, then.

30
00:02:44.331 --> 00:02:45.541
See ya!

31
00:02:46.876 --> 00:02:47.877
That punk.

32
00:03:00.931 --> 00:03:01.765
Young-joo!

33
00:03:09.231 --> 00:03:10.190
Young-joo.

34
00:03:15.738 --> 00:03:16.780
Young-joo.

35
00:03:17.865 --> 00:03:21.243
Young-joo!

36
00:03:25.247 --> 00:03:26.248
Young-joo!

37
00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:29.335
Young-joo!

38
00:03:35.257 --> 00:03:39.053
Young-joo!

39
00:03:40.012 --> 00:03:41.055
Young-joo!

40
00:03:41.388 --> 00:03:44.266
Young-joo!

41
00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:48.812
1ST PLATOON LEE JAE-YOON

42
00:04:01.617 --> 00:04:02.493
Salute.

43
00:04:02.952 --> 00:04:05.453
- Keep it down. You'll wake the others.
- Yes, sir.

44
00:04:05.454 --> 00:04:07.915
- Wake In-ho and prepare for duty.
- Yes, sir.

45
00:04:08.624 --> 00:04:09.458
It's coming.

46
00:04:10.417 --> 00:04:11.752
It's headed this way, sir.

47
00:04:13.337 --> 00:04:14.296
In-ho.

48
00:04:14.672 --> 00:04:15.922
Wake up. It's our shift.

49
00:04:15.923 --> 00:04:18.549
Looks like a single US F-100.

50
00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:20.551
Subtle retreat at wing roots.

51
00:04:20.552 --> 00:04:22.971
- Blunt nose, like a sausage--
- In-ho.

52
00:04:22.972 --> 00:04:25.056
The nose is circular. A circular engine.

53
00:04:25.057 --> 00:04:26.517
Beware of circular hair loss.

54
00:04:26.976 --> 00:04:28.226
What did you say?

55
00:04:28.227 --> 00:04:31.813
Thousands of bombers
are heading toward us.

56
00:04:31.814 --> 00:04:33.773
I think he can hear us.

57
00:04:33.774 --> 00:04:34.942
Yes, sir.

58
00:04:36.735 --> 00:04:37.777
How close are they?

59
00:04:37.778 --> 00:04:39.070
They're under our noses.

60
00:04:39.071 --> 00:04:40.405
Watch out. They will crash.

61
00:04:40.406 --> 00:04:42.824
Watch out! They're headed straight for us!

62
00:04:42.825 --> 00:04:45.494
Corporal Ra In-ho!

63
00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:47.788
When did you become a corporal?

64
00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:50.916
I don't follow, sir.

65
00:04:53.252 --> 00:04:55.879
Oh, right. I'm not a corporal yet.

66
00:04:57.131 --> 00:05:00.009
Private Ra In-ho!

67
00:05:00.592 --> 00:05:02.928
This guy's a total washout.

68
00:05:03.345 --> 00:05:04.762
Get ready to stand guard.

69
00:05:04.763 --> 00:05:05.973
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir.

70
00:06:14.041 --> 00:06:15.876
{\an8}MY DARLING YOUNG-JOO

71
00:06:34.144 --> 00:06:39.983
SWEET JAE-YOON

72
00:06:47.658 --> 00:06:49.660
What?

73
00:06:49.993 --> 00:06:50.994
Answer your phone.

74
00:06:54.081 --> 00:06:56.166
Tell him if he calls at this hour again,

75
00:06:56.583 --> 00:06:59.044
I won't let you date him anymore.

76
00:07:06.593 --> 00:07:07.593
<i>Hello?</i>

77
00:07:07.594 --> 00:07:10.055
- Hello?
<i>- What is going on?</i>

78
00:07:10.764 --> 00:07:12.932
Hi, Jae-yoon. What's up?

79
00:07:12.933 --> 00:07:14.017
<i>"What's up"?</i>

80
00:07:15.352 --> 00:07:17.895
<i>- That's what you have to say?</i>
- Yes.

81
00:07:17.896 --> 00:07:19.188
<i>Young-joo.</i>

82
00:07:19.189 --> 00:07:21.441
<i>Getting drunk is one thing.</i>

83
00:07:21.942 --> 00:07:24.569
But I couldn't
get a hold of you for hours,

84
00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:27.656
and then some random guy
picked up your phone.

85
00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:31.325
So, what the hell is going on?

86
00:07:31.326 --> 00:07:34.328
I think you talked to my manager.

87
00:07:34.329 --> 00:07:37.623
He brought me home because I was drunk.

88
00:07:37.624 --> 00:07:41.210
- A guy brought you home?
<i>- Yes.</i>

89
00:07:41.211 --> 00:07:44.046
You got hammered
and let some guy take you...

90
00:07:44.047 --> 00:07:46.340
<i>Kang Young-joo,
do you not think of me at all?</i>

91
00:07:46.341 --> 00:07:49.720
I'm always thinking of you.

92
00:07:51.346 --> 00:07:52.598
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

93
00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:55.058
But Jae-yoon, it's...

94
00:07:56.393 --> 00:07:58.353
It's 3 a.m. right now.

95
00:07:58.687 --> 00:08:01.314
<i>Even if I'm terribly in the wrong,</i>

96
00:08:01.315 --> 00:08:05.651
calling and waking me up
at this time of night isn't right either.

97
00:08:05.652 --> 00:08:09.071
I couldn't sleep a wink
because I was worried sick about you.

98
00:08:09.072 --> 00:08:11.407
<i>Okay, fine.</i>

99
00:08:11.408 --> 00:08:14.619
<i>I'm sorry for not picking up
or messaging you.</i>

100
00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:17.706
I'll explain everything
tomorrow morning...

101
00:08:22.002 --> 00:08:23.003
<i>Hello?</i>

102
00:08:23.629 --> 00:08:24.671
<i>Hello?</i>

103
00:08:25.005 --> 00:08:25.880
<i>What happened?</i>

104
00:08:25.881 --> 00:08:27.716
<i>Hello? Young-joo.</i>

105
00:08:28.008 --> 00:08:29.008
<i>Hello?</i>

106
00:08:29.009 --> 00:08:30.302
Young-joo? Hello?

107
00:08:31.845 --> 00:08:33.555
What the heck?

108
00:08:34.181 --> 00:08:35.640
I won't let it slide this time.

109
00:08:35.641 --> 00:08:36.975
What is she thinking?

110
00:08:37.392 --> 00:08:38.810
My thoughts exactly.

111
00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:46.443
- Salute.
- I can't let this slide, either.

112
00:08:49.696 --> 00:08:51.989
Look at him for fuck's sake.

113
00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:54.116
What should I do with you two?

114
00:08:54.117 --> 00:08:56.078
I finished my meal, sir.

115
00:09:02.626 --> 00:09:03.710
Salute.

116
00:09:04.294 --> 00:09:05.212
Salute.

117
00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:07.630
May 2nd, 2025.

118
00:09:07.631 --> 00:09:08.965
First Platoon morning roll call.

119
00:09:08.966 --> 00:09:11.092
Of the nine members, two are on duty.

120
00:09:11.093 --> 00:09:14.011
The remaining seven are present.

121
00:09:14.012 --> 00:09:15.013
Report complete.

122
00:09:15.347 --> 00:09:17.015
- At ease.
- At ease.

123
00:09:18.392 --> 00:09:19.268
At ease.

124
00:09:19.977 --> 00:09:23.771
The CO canceled
today's national pledge and training.

125
00:09:23.772 --> 00:09:26.733
It's easy to tense up
and strain your muscles in this cold.

126
00:09:28.068 --> 00:09:30.486
So, don't stay indoors
and watch TV all day.

127
00:09:30.487 --> 00:09:33.656
Do some basic exercise
to keep fit. That's all.

128
00:09:33.657 --> 00:09:35.783
- Salute.
- Salute!

129
00:09:35.784 --> 00:09:36.910
Salute.

130
00:09:38.787 --> 00:09:40.789
Who is that dozing off?

131
00:09:42.082 --> 00:09:43.416
Is this the best you can do?

132
00:09:43.417 --> 00:09:44.834
- No, sir!
- No, sir!

133
00:09:44.835 --> 00:09:47.004
You're in your prime. Act like it!

134
00:09:48.088 --> 00:09:50.716
- Squad commander.
- Yes, sir.

135
00:09:51.258 --> 00:09:53.593
Have them do 50 laps
around the training ground.

136
00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:56.012
Are you complaining?

137
00:09:56.013 --> 00:09:57.180
You punks.

138
00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:00.099
Do you want to do 80 laps?

139
00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.601
- No, sir!
- No, sir!

140
00:10:05.314 --> 00:10:07.732
Let's make it 67 laps.

141
00:10:07.733 --> 00:10:08.774
Get to it.

142
00:10:08.775 --> 00:10:10.694
- Get to it.
- Yes, sir!

143
00:10:12.321 --> 00:10:14.740
There are fewer than ten of you,
and you can't run in sync?

144
00:10:15.407 --> 00:10:17.116
Fall into step!

145
00:10:17.117 --> 00:10:19.786
Left.

146
00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:21.288
Left.

147
00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:24.416
- One, two...
- Sixty-five laps to go!

148
00:10:24.833 --> 00:10:26.960
Three, four.

149
00:10:27.961 --> 00:10:32.798
One, two, three, four.

150
00:10:32.799 --> 00:10:34.508
- One, two, three, four.
- Sync up!

151
00:10:34.509 --> 00:10:36.260
March in time!

152
00:10:36.261 --> 00:10:40.015
- One, two, three...
- One, two, three...

153
00:10:58.158 --> 00:10:59.743
SWEET JAE-YOON

154
00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:02.244
Kang Young-joo. Wait up.

155
00:11:02.245 --> 00:11:03.955
Hi. We're late. Let's run.

156
00:11:06.166 --> 00:11:08.209
{\an8}EXIT

157
00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:09.585
{\an8}ENTRANCE

158
00:11:09.586 --> 00:11:11.504
{\an8}- Young-joo.
- Hello.

159
00:11:11.505 --> 00:11:12.923
- You just got here?
- Yes.

160
00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:15.926
- Hello.
- Long time no see, Seul-gi.

161
00:11:16.802 --> 00:11:18.177
How's work so far?

162
00:11:18.178 --> 00:11:21.181
I'm settling in really fast,
thanks to your help.

163
00:11:21.807 --> 00:11:23.099
I owe you.

164
00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:25.476
You've been saying that

165
00:11:25.477 --> 00:11:27.104
since you joined a month ago.

166
00:11:27.979 --> 00:11:32.359
Put your money where your mouth is
and buy me <i>tteokbokki,</i> at least.

167
00:11:33.902 --> 00:11:37.864
I could buy you
a hundred servings of <i>tteokbokki.</i>

168
00:11:38.281 --> 00:11:40.617
Really? How about today, then?

169
00:11:41.618 --> 00:11:42.786
Today?

170
00:11:43.829 --> 00:11:45.205
Today...

171
00:11:46.623 --> 00:11:48.250
It's okay if you're busy.

172
00:11:49.459 --> 00:11:50.544
Next week's fine too.

173
00:11:53.547 --> 00:11:55.215
<i>The doors are closing.</i>

174
00:12:02.139 --> 00:12:04.224
SWEET JAE-YOON

175
00:12:07.477 --> 00:12:09.396
MY DARLING YOUNG-JOO

176
00:12:15.819 --> 00:12:19.489
<i>The person you are
trying to reach is unavailable.</i>

177
00:12:19.865 --> 00:12:21.824
<i>Please try again later.</i>

178
00:12:21.825 --> 00:12:23.618
Seriously?

179
00:12:24.786 --> 00:12:26.871
<i>Air defense emergency.</i>

180
00:12:26.872 --> 00:12:29.416
<i>Gear up and assemble in five minutes.</i>

181
00:12:29.749 --> 00:12:32.418
An emergency this early in the day?

182
00:12:32.419 --> 00:12:33.628
Why?

183
00:12:35.464 --> 00:12:36.590
Salute!

184
00:12:37.507 --> 00:12:38.508
This way, sir.

185
00:12:41.344 --> 00:12:42.595
We'll begin, sir.

186
00:12:42.596 --> 00:12:43.638
Proceed.

187
00:12:44.764 --> 00:12:48.976
One Mi-4 approaching the base
at 8 o'clock, 7 klicks out.

188
00:12:48.977 --> 00:12:52.021
Approval given to fire at target
and shoot it down.

189
00:12:52.022 --> 00:12:54.690
One Mi-4 approaching
at 8 o'clock, 7 klicks out.

190
00:12:54.691 --> 00:12:57.152
Approval given to fire at target
and shoot it down!

191
00:12:57.903 --> 00:12:59.111
Signal Unit. Lift the receiver.

192
00:12:59.112 --> 00:13:01.030
Press the red button.
Standby three seconds.

193
00:13:01.031 --> 00:13:02.573
Air defense emergency.

194
00:13:02.574 --> 00:13:04.408
One Mi-4 approaching
at 8 o'clock, 7 klicks out.

195
00:13:04.409 --> 00:13:06.368
Approval given to fire at target
and shoot it down.

196
00:13:06.369 --> 00:13:07.453
Air defense emergency.

197
00:13:07.454 --> 00:13:09.663
One Mi-4 approaching
at 8 o'clock, 7 klicks out.

198
00:13:09.664 --> 00:13:12.458
Approval given to fire at target
and shoot it down.

199
00:13:12.459 --> 00:13:13.543
Generator on.

200
00:13:16.296 --> 00:13:17.631
Connection secure.

201
00:13:18.215 --> 00:13:20.132
Officer in charge, Jeon Hyung-bae!

202
00:13:20.133 --> 00:13:21.342
Sights open!

203
00:13:21.343 --> 00:13:23.427
- Unlock and switch on.
- Unlock and switch on.

204
00:13:23.428 --> 00:13:25.095
- Power on.
- Power on.

205
00:13:25.096 --> 00:13:26.972
- Firing speed 30.
- Firing speed 30.

206
00:13:26.973 --> 00:13:30.142
- Fire one simulated round via radar.
- One simulated round via radar.

207
00:13:30.143 --> 00:13:34.897
Target is at 8 o'clock, 7 klicks.
Disperse around the barrel.

208
00:13:34.898 --> 00:13:36.982
- Target locked at 7 klicks.
- Target locked at 7 klicks.

209
00:13:36.983 --> 00:13:38.150
- Six klicks.
- Six klicks!

210
00:13:38.151 --> 00:13:40.027
- Target locked at 5 klicks.
- Target locked at 5.

211
00:13:40.028 --> 00:13:41.111
- Four klicks.
- Four klicks!

212
00:13:41.112 --> 00:13:42.488
- Three klicks.
- Three klicks!

213
00:13:42.489 --> 00:13:45.242
One, two, aim and fire!

214
00:13:49.955 --> 00:13:50.956
Power off.

215
00:13:51.873 --> 00:13:53.457
- Attack report.
- Report!

216
00:13:53.458 --> 00:13:54.959
Target has been neutralized.

217
00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:57.211
Thirty rounds fired.
No issues with personnel or equipment.

218
00:13:57.212 --> 00:13:58.421
Roger.

219
00:14:09.224 --> 00:14:10.350
Ammo Dump One open!

220
00:14:10.934 --> 00:14:11.767
Ammo Dump Two open!

221
00:14:11.768 --> 00:14:13.060
- One hundred rounds!
- One hundred rounds!

222
00:14:13.061 --> 00:14:14.103
- Two hundred!
- Two hundred!

223
00:14:14.104 --> 00:14:15.272
- Three hundred!
- Three hundred!

224
00:14:20.068 --> 00:14:22.236
- Armed and ready!
- Armed and ready!

225
00:14:22.237 --> 00:14:24.780
Here's your order!

226
00:14:24.781 --> 00:14:26.031
The direction is...

227
00:14:26.032 --> 00:14:27.075
Base...

228
00:14:27.867 --> 00:14:30.870
One o'clock, five klicks,
An-2, paratroopers.

229
00:14:31.538 --> 00:14:34.331
At 1 o'clock, 5 klicks out,
an An-2 is dropping paratroopers.

230
00:14:34.332 --> 00:14:36.668
Prepare artillery to target them.

231
00:14:37.377 --> 00:14:38.503
And report.

232
00:14:39.671 --> 00:14:42.006
Report on the firing.

233
00:14:42.007 --> 00:14:43.382
<i>- Roger.</i>
- Roger!

234
00:14:43.383 --> 00:14:44.925
<i>- Roger.</i>
- Run.

235
00:14:44.926 --> 00:14:46.844
- Power on.
- Power on.

236
00:14:46.845 --> 00:14:50.848
Target at 1 o'clock, 5 klicks.
Disperse around the barrel.

237
00:14:50.849 --> 00:14:52.641
- Manual targeting.
- Manual targeting.

238
00:14:52.642 --> 00:14:54.727
- Slow rate of fire.
- Firing speed, low.

239
00:14:54.728 --> 00:14:56.520
- Target speed zero.
- Target speed zero.

240
00:14:56.521 --> 00:14:58.564
- Distance to target, 2,000.
- Distance to target, 2,000.

241
00:14:58.565 --> 00:15:00.858
- Target acquired.
- Target acquired.

242
00:15:00.859 --> 00:15:02.776
- Platform switch on.
- Confirmed.

243
00:15:02.777 --> 00:15:04.028
One, two, aim and fire!

244
00:15:04.029 --> 00:15:06.238
- One, two, aim and fire. Bang.
- One, two, aim and fire. Bang.

245
00:15:06.239 --> 00:15:08.073
- Locked on target!
- Locked on target.

246
00:15:08.074 --> 00:15:09.992
- Platform switch on.
- Confirmed.

247
00:15:09.993 --> 00:15:12.077
- One, two, aim and fire!
- One, two, aim and fire!

248
00:15:12.078 --> 00:15:13.496
- Bang.
- Bang.

249
00:15:14.623 --> 00:15:15.581
Power off.

250
00:15:15.582 --> 00:15:18.042
Paratroopers were shot down,
90 shots were fired.

251
00:15:18.043 --> 00:15:19.961
- No issues with personnel or equipment.
- Roger.

252
00:15:20.879 --> 00:15:23.048
Those two are our best men.

253
00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:25.758
And ammunition bearer,
Private Hwang Kyung-sik,

254
00:15:25.759 --> 00:15:28.761
came first in the tenth
Division Commander Shooting Competition.

255
00:15:28.762 --> 00:15:31.097
He's one of the men we're training up.

256
00:15:34.517 --> 00:15:36.102
First Lieutenant Park Sung-wook.

257
00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:39.898
The KP-SAM is over there.

258
00:15:45.654 --> 00:15:47.614
We got the guided missile!

259
00:16:08.426 --> 00:16:10.512
Boom!

260
00:16:11.054 --> 00:16:13.682
We're all dead!

261
00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:18.269
Those two

262
00:16:18.853 --> 00:16:20.854
are older than the rest.

263
00:16:20.855 --> 00:16:22.357
They're 26 and 30 years old.

264
00:16:22.982 --> 00:16:25.610
So, they're having a little trouble

265
00:16:26.319 --> 00:16:28.071
getting used to the military...

266
00:16:33.868 --> 00:16:35.078
"We're all dead."

267
00:16:36.955 --> 00:16:39.207
- Squad commander.
- Yes, sir.

268
00:16:40.583 --> 00:16:42.043
What is our mission?

269
00:16:42.711 --> 00:16:44.378
To defend against unexpected enemy attacks

270
00:16:44.379 --> 00:16:46.839
by establishing an outpost
equipped with anti-aircraft guns

271
00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.758
on Tower 77A,
the highest vantage point in Seoul,

272
00:16:49.759 --> 00:16:52.720
safeguard the city's key infrastructure,
protect the citizens,

273
00:16:52.721 --> 00:16:55.473
and secure the airspace over our capital.

274
00:16:57.934 --> 00:16:59.144
Forward, march.

275
00:17:03.398 --> 00:17:04.649
Halt.

276
00:17:05.525 --> 00:17:06.526
About face.

277
00:17:08.153 --> 00:17:11.740
You have all let me down today.

278
00:17:13.199 --> 00:17:16.077
I should write you all up
for disciplinary action.

279
00:17:16.661 --> 00:17:19.121
Be grateful I'm ending it at this.

280
00:17:19.122 --> 00:17:20.415
There are 77 floors.

281
00:17:20.957 --> 00:17:24.669
Climb to the top
and think about what you did wrong.

282
00:17:26.463 --> 00:17:27.380
Salute.

283
00:17:27.964 --> 00:17:29.174
Damn it.

284
00:17:32.385 --> 00:17:34.344
I'd rather receive disciplinary action.

285
00:17:34.345 --> 00:17:35.888
Seventy-seven floors...

286
00:17:35.889 --> 00:17:37.432
Shut your fucking mouths!

287
00:17:39.768 --> 00:17:40.727
About face.

288
00:17:43.813 --> 00:17:45.398
Forward, march.

289
00:18:09.881 --> 00:18:11.007
Watch out.

290
00:18:12.091 --> 00:18:13.927
We need to stay on schedule.

291
00:18:26.147 --> 00:18:27.315
Shit!

292
00:18:29.067 --> 00:18:30.610
Mom, I'm hungry.

293
00:18:31.319 --> 00:18:35.365
- Still? We had a big breakfast.
- I'm still hungry.

294
00:18:55.218 --> 00:18:56.261
Private Lee Jae-yoon.

295
00:18:57.345 --> 00:18:58.554
I'm a lost cause.

296
00:18:58.555 --> 00:19:00.222
- Keep going.
- Leave me behind.

297
00:19:00.223 --> 00:19:01.432
Keep going, punk.

298
00:19:02.225 --> 00:19:03.309
Kim Young-man.

299
00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:06.354
I bet you're coasting
now that you're a sergeant.

300
00:19:07.647 --> 00:19:09.273
If you don't manage your men,

301
00:19:09.274 --> 00:19:12.192
people will think
you're pissing around, you moron.

302
00:19:12.193 --> 00:19:13.486
I'll do better, sir.

303
00:19:22.412 --> 00:19:24.038
Look at those bastards.

304
00:19:27.584 --> 00:19:28.835
Push-up positions.

305
00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:30.378
Hey!

306
00:19:30.879 --> 00:19:32.005
Push-up positions!

307
00:19:37.677 --> 00:19:39.804
In-ho and Jae-yoon, you bastards.

308
00:19:42.724 --> 00:19:44.142
Just last night,

309
00:19:44.642 --> 00:19:47.061
I caught one punk
using his phone on guard duty.

310
00:19:47.812 --> 00:19:50.273
And the other was fast asleep.

311
00:19:50.607 --> 00:19:53.150
As if that wasn't enough,
during emergency training,

312
00:19:53.151 --> 00:19:54.777
a gunner dropped a missile

313
00:19:55.486 --> 00:19:57.071
in front of our battalion commander.

314
00:19:58.907 --> 00:20:01.284
And I realized

315
00:20:01.743 --> 00:20:03.953
that our platoon is in shit shape.

316
00:20:04.871 --> 00:20:06.956
If I were the battalion commander,

317
00:20:08.166 --> 00:20:11.336
all you bastards would be in the brig!

318
00:20:11.628 --> 00:20:12.462
You hear me?

319
00:20:16.925 --> 00:20:18.426
From this moment on,

320
00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:20.886
you're banned from using your phones.

321
00:20:20.887 --> 00:20:23.305
If I catch anyone using their phone,

322
00:20:23.306 --> 00:20:26.017
I'll kill him and go to the brig myself.

323
00:20:27.018 --> 00:20:28.685
- Hyung-bae.
- Yes, sir.

324
00:20:28.686 --> 00:20:30.104
- Take their phones.
- Yes, sir.

325
00:20:32.023 --> 00:20:33.023
And you two.

326
00:20:33.024 --> 00:20:35.275
Private First Class,
Lee Jae-yoon, reporting.

327
00:20:35.276 --> 00:20:37.946
Private Ra In-ho, reporting.

328
00:20:40.823 --> 00:20:43.575
I really didn't want
to say this to you two.

329
00:20:43.576 --> 00:20:46.203
But you're older than the rest of us,

330
00:20:46.204 --> 00:20:47.788
so act your age.

331
00:20:47.789 --> 00:20:49.332
You bastards.

332
00:20:53.378 --> 00:20:57.256
<i>I couldn't pick up because I overslept
and had to rush to work.</i>

333
00:20:58.591 --> 00:21:00.593
<i>I'm so sorry about yesterday, Jae-yoon.</i>

334
00:21:01.844 --> 00:21:05.431
<i>I had too much to drink
at the newbie welcome dinner.</i>

335
00:21:07.850 --> 00:21:11.813
<i>My manager and supervisor
dropped me off since they live nearby.</i>

336
00:21:12.689 --> 00:21:15.108
<i>I totally get why you would
get the wrong idea.</i>

337
00:21:18.194 --> 00:21:19.445
<i>But Jae-yoon...</i>

338
00:21:21.572 --> 00:21:23.281
Private Choi Chul-woo.

339
00:21:23.282 --> 00:21:24.409
Private Hwang Kyung-sik.

340
00:21:25.952 --> 00:21:26.868
Move it.

341
00:21:26.869 --> 00:21:28.120
Private Ra In-ho.

342
00:21:28.121 --> 00:21:29.121
- Go.
- Yes, sir.

343
00:21:29.122 --> 00:21:30.248
You moron.

344
00:21:31.165 --> 00:21:32.625
Private Lee Jae-yoon.

345
00:21:34.377 --> 00:21:35.211
{\an8}Let go.

346
00:21:35.712 --> 00:21:37.338
{\an8}- Just a moment.
- Let go.

347
00:21:38.381 --> 00:21:39.340
- Just one second--
- Hey.

348
00:21:40.049 --> 00:21:41.509
It's a really important text.

349
00:21:42.301 --> 00:21:43.720
Damn it, Jae-yoon.

350
00:21:44.095 --> 00:21:45.054
Let go right now.

351
00:21:46.097 --> 00:21:48.557
Get it together. This is all your fault.

352
00:21:48.558 --> 00:21:49.600
I'm sorry, sir.

353
00:21:55.023 --> 00:21:58.067
- Salute.
- Salute.

354
00:21:59.986 --> 00:22:01.778
What's with the vibe in here?

355
00:22:01.779 --> 00:22:03.739
I feel like I'm walking on eggshells.

356
00:22:03.740 --> 00:22:04.699
What are you doing?

357
00:22:05.241 --> 00:22:06.576
Private Choi Chul-woo, reporting.

358
00:22:07.410 --> 00:22:10.287
After climbing all those stairs,
you still want to work out?

359
00:22:10.288 --> 00:22:12.040
Why are your arms so huge?

360
00:22:12.874 --> 00:22:15.460
You need to work your upper body
after a leg workout.

361
00:22:16.461 --> 00:22:18.545
Just looking at you exhausts me.

362
00:22:18.546 --> 00:22:21.506
I'll give you some boiled chicken breast.
Come to the mess hall later.

363
00:22:21.507 --> 00:22:22.633
Yes, Corporal Kwak.

364
00:22:23.593 --> 00:22:24.551
Thank you, sir!

365
00:22:24.552 --> 00:22:26.678
- Kwak, give me your phone.
- What?

366
00:22:26.679 --> 00:22:28.056
Oh, sure.

367
00:22:28.556 --> 00:22:30.724
It never rings anyway. Take it.

368
00:22:30.725 --> 00:22:31.642
But, in return,

369
00:22:32.560 --> 00:22:34.644
I need someone to help with the cooking.

370
00:22:34.645 --> 00:22:38.232
I have to make a delivery.
How much longer must I do this for?

371
00:22:40.026 --> 00:22:41.569
Why is he the only one who's not beat?

372
00:22:41.944 --> 00:22:42.779
That moron.

373
00:22:43.112 --> 00:22:45.363
- I'll take Jae-yoon.
- Private Lee Jae-yoon, reporting!

374
00:22:45.364 --> 00:22:46.949
- You're helping me.
- Yes, sir!

375
00:22:49.535 --> 00:22:50.661
Move faster.

376
00:23:06.511 --> 00:23:07.969
Unbelievable.

377
00:23:07.970 --> 00:23:09.262
First Sergeant Jung
and First Lieutenant Park

378
00:23:09.263 --> 00:23:12.682
always go on about how
the system needs to be cleaned up.

379
00:23:12.683 --> 00:23:14.768
But they always make me bring them food

380
00:23:14.769 --> 00:23:17.105
so they won't have to eat
the same slop we do.

381
00:23:17.980 --> 00:23:20.315
Talk about double standards.
Just wait and see.

382
00:23:20.316 --> 00:23:22.652
Before I'm discharged, I'll report them.

383
00:23:22.985 --> 00:23:24.027
Isn't that funny?

384
00:23:24.028 --> 00:23:25.113
You punk.

385
00:23:26.447 --> 00:23:28.323
Am I talking to myself?

386
00:23:28.324 --> 00:23:29.408
Say something.

387
00:23:29.951 --> 00:23:31.077
I'm sorry, sir.

388
00:23:32.745 --> 00:23:36.374
You know, you and In-ho are a liability.

389
00:23:36.749 --> 00:23:38.375
Even today, the both of you--

390
00:23:38.376 --> 00:23:40.168
In-ho makes more mistakes than I--

391
00:23:40.169 --> 00:23:42.462
Why can't either of you
get the hang of things?

392
00:23:42.463 --> 00:23:44.256
In-ho's clearly not the sharpest tool,

393
00:23:44.257 --> 00:23:46.341
and he's older
than the rest of us, so I get it.

394
00:23:46.342 --> 00:23:49.219
But you attend a top-tier university
and look like a smart...

395
00:23:49.220 --> 00:23:50.555
What is it?

396
00:23:51.222 --> 00:23:52.181
Is there a problem?

397
00:23:54.225 --> 00:23:55.434
Those people...

398
00:24:02.358 --> 00:24:03.568
What about those people?

399
00:24:05.820 --> 00:24:06.737
It's nothing, sir.

400
00:24:09.407 --> 00:24:11.158
You being here is a problem.

401
00:24:11.159 --> 00:24:12.201
Let's hurry.

402
00:24:32.722 --> 00:24:35.098
- Hey, what are you looking at?
- I just...

403
00:24:35.099 --> 00:24:36.725
- Get over here.
- Sorry, sir.

404
00:24:36.726 --> 00:24:38.811
- Shit, are you Ra In-ho?
- No, sir.

405
00:24:39.520 --> 00:24:40.937
Hey, do it now.

406
00:24:40.938 --> 00:24:41.939
Attention.

407
00:24:43.983 --> 00:24:45.151
Hello, Soo-jeong.

408
00:24:45.776 --> 00:24:50.364
We installed an elevator
exclusively for you.

409
00:24:50.781 --> 00:24:53.867
Your presence will upset the VIP guests.

410
00:24:53.868 --> 00:24:55.243
Oh, dear.

411
00:24:55.244 --> 00:24:56.286
You haven't heard.

412
00:24:56.287 --> 00:24:58.371
That elevator is out of order.

413
00:24:58.372 --> 00:25:01.374
Then, you should have reported it.

414
00:25:01.375 --> 00:25:04.420
Our phones were confiscated.
Can you believe it?

415
00:25:10.760 --> 00:25:11.761
Anyway.

416
00:25:12.511 --> 00:25:14.930
Please follow our instructions.

417
00:25:14.931 --> 00:25:16.515
- Please.
- Sure. Sorry.

418
00:25:17.683 --> 00:25:19.935
In case this happens again,

419
00:25:19.936 --> 00:25:23.021
I think it'd be best
if we could contact you directly.

420
00:25:23.022 --> 00:25:24.856
Could you give me a business card?

421
00:25:24.857 --> 00:25:25.941
Soo-jeong?

422
00:25:25.942 --> 00:25:28.068
What the heck are you on about?

423
00:25:28.069 --> 00:25:30.738
Why the hell would I give you
my business card?

424
00:25:31.405 --> 00:25:32.739
- Goodness gracious.
- What?

425
00:25:32.740 --> 00:25:35.951
Are you this cold to everyone?

426
00:25:35.952 --> 00:25:36.994
You lunatic...

427
00:25:39.580 --> 00:25:42.123
Just do your thing and get lost.

428
00:25:42.124 --> 00:25:43.959
You have no business with me.

429
00:25:43.960 --> 00:25:46.253
- No, my business is right here.
- What?

430
00:25:46.254 --> 00:25:47.713
Do you remember my name?

431
00:25:48.339 --> 00:25:50.298
Why should I remember your name?

432
00:25:50.299 --> 00:25:51.841
It's right here. Kwak Gye-young.

433
00:25:51.842 --> 00:25:54.010
You don't seem to get the message.

434
00:25:54.011 --> 00:25:55.470
- It's not the first time--
- Excuse me.

435
00:25:55.471 --> 00:25:56.388
Jae-yoon.

436
00:25:56.389 --> 00:25:58.014
- Yes?
- It's the man of legend, Arron Park.

437
00:25:58.015 --> 00:25:59.099
- Retreat.
- Hey.

438
00:25:59.100 --> 00:26:00.393
- It's Arron Park.
- Hey!

439
00:26:08.651 --> 00:26:10.152
Those little shits.

440
00:26:11.904 --> 00:26:13.239
Arron Park...

441
00:26:14.115 --> 00:26:16.158
He almost caught us. Darn it.

442
00:26:18.953 --> 00:26:21.079
- Things were going so well.
- What a shame.

443
00:26:21.080 --> 00:26:23.541
- Let's drop this off and get out.
- Yes, sir.

444
00:27:00.328 --> 00:27:02.788
Speak of the devil.

445
00:27:04.290 --> 00:27:05.498
Let's cut some meat.

446
00:27:05.499 --> 00:27:07.292
Look forward
to the Korean banquet tomorrow.

447
00:27:07.293 --> 00:27:08.376
- A banquet?
- Hi, Jae-yoon.

448
00:27:08.377 --> 00:27:09.503
For real?

449
00:27:10.004 --> 00:27:11.629
I'll have dinner down here, then.

450
00:27:11.630 --> 00:27:13.424
Me too.

451
00:27:21.682 --> 00:27:23.224
<i>- Ttukbaegi.
- "Ttukbaegi"?</i>

452
00:27:23.225 --> 00:27:24.976
<i>What's local is best</i>

453
00:27:24.977 --> 00:27:27.729
Corporal. I need to speak with Chef Jung.

454
00:27:27.730 --> 00:27:29.230
- Get back in five minutes.
- Yes, sir.

455
00:27:29.231 --> 00:27:30.982
The first sergeant
will freak if we're late--

456
00:27:30.983 --> 00:27:32.401
- I know, sir!
- What a punk.

457
00:27:34.153 --> 00:27:35.528
{\an8}<i>Ongojishin.</i>

458
00:27:35.529 --> 00:27:36.988
{\an8}KNOW THE OLD TO LEARN THE NEW

459
00:27:36.989 --> 00:27:38.032
Here.

460
00:27:38.699 --> 00:27:40.576
Use it freely, Private First Class Lee.

461
00:27:42.328 --> 00:27:44.454
I'll remember this until the day I die.

462
00:27:44.455 --> 00:27:45.664
Thank you.

463
00:27:46.374 --> 00:27:47.583
Thank you.

464
00:27:59.178 --> 00:28:01.555
Young-joo, your phone's ringing.

465
00:28:04.266 --> 00:28:05.601
You ate your shrimp already?

466
00:28:07.853 --> 00:28:08.853
Hello?

467
00:28:08.854 --> 00:28:10.356
<i>Kang Young-joo!</i>

468
00:28:11.440 --> 00:28:14.527
<i>You said you'd explain
in the morning, but you didn't pick up!</i>

469
00:28:15.694 --> 00:28:17.571
Oh, hey, Jae-yoon.

470
00:28:17.947 --> 00:28:18.988
Whose phone is this?

471
00:28:18.989 --> 00:28:21.825
<i>That's not what's important.
I'm really angry.</i>

472
00:28:21.826 --> 00:28:24.412
<i>Are you going to keep dodging the issue?</i>

473
00:28:26.122 --> 00:28:28.666
<i>I bet you were too wasted
to even remember last night's call.</i>

474
00:28:29.041 --> 00:28:30.501
<i>- Am I right?</i>
- Hey.

475
00:28:30.835 --> 00:28:32.961
I explained everything in the text.

476
00:28:32.962 --> 00:28:36.548
<i>Are you seriously trying to brush this off
with one text message?</i>

477
00:28:36.549 --> 00:28:39.217
<i>Do you not get what the problem is?</i>

478
00:28:39.218 --> 00:28:40.511
Okay, fine.

479
00:28:40.970 --> 00:28:41.970
Last night--

480
00:28:41.971 --> 00:28:44.097
<i>The first sergeant asked for me,
so we have to go,</i>

481
00:28:44.098 --> 00:28:46.434
<i>- or I'll end up in the brig!
- Yes, sir!</i>

482
00:28:46.892 --> 00:28:49.310
<i>I'll call you right back.
Explain everything then. Got it?</i>

483
00:28:49.311 --> 00:28:50.396
Hey, Jae-yoon.

484
00:28:58.737 --> 00:29:00.197
Was that your soldier boyfriend?

485
00:29:01.115 --> 00:29:02.449
- Yes.
- I see.

486
00:29:02.450 --> 00:29:03.659
What's his rank?

487
00:29:04.076 --> 00:29:05.828
- He's a private.
- Oh, dear.

488
00:29:06.287 --> 00:29:07.538
He has ages left.

489
00:29:08.831 --> 00:29:09.789
Will you wait for him?

490
00:29:09.790 --> 00:29:12.959
Why would you even ask?

491
00:29:12.960 --> 00:29:14.336
She's not stupid.

492
00:29:14.837 --> 00:29:17.088
Why would she waste time
waiting for someone she won't marry?

493
00:29:17.089 --> 00:29:18.174
Right?

494
00:29:20.676 --> 00:29:21.801
Is it a waste of time?

495
00:29:21.802 --> 00:29:23.887
- Of course.
- What's wrong with you?

496
00:29:23.888 --> 00:29:27.308
Maybe she loves him enough
to marry him once he's discharged.

497
00:29:29.018 --> 00:29:30.477
Right, Young-joo?

498
00:29:30.478 --> 00:29:32.563
You're thinking of marrying him, right?

499
00:29:36.400 --> 00:29:38.693
I haven't given it that much thought.

500
00:29:38.694 --> 00:29:39.612
Time out.

501
00:29:40.070 --> 00:29:41.906
You should start thinking now.

502
00:29:43.115 --> 00:29:45.868
You're not exactly young anymore.

503
00:29:46.368 --> 00:29:48.370
Why would you say that?

504
00:29:49.121 --> 00:29:50.163
What's your problem?

505
00:29:50.164 --> 00:29:51.956
What I mean is,

506
00:29:51.957 --> 00:29:55.084
you're of the age
to be thinking about these things.

507
00:29:55.085 --> 00:29:56.377
I'm just kidding.

508
00:29:56.378 --> 00:29:58.380
He's right. You should think about it.

509
00:30:00.424 --> 00:30:01.883
I've got it handled.

510
00:30:01.884 --> 00:30:03.384
Please, eat up.

511
00:30:03.385 --> 00:30:05.137
I don't feel well.

512
00:30:07.097 --> 00:30:08.349
Enjoy your meals.

513
00:30:24.240 --> 00:30:25.241
<i>Hello?</i>

514
00:30:26.867 --> 00:30:30.746
Can I speak with Private Lee Jae-yoon?

515
00:30:31.872 --> 00:30:34.750
<i>I'm sorry. He returned to his unit.</i>

516
00:30:37.545 --> 00:30:39.547
- Okay, then.
<i>- Bye.</i>

517
00:31:00.818 --> 00:31:01.819
Ra In-ho.

518
00:31:04.280 --> 00:31:05.405
Private Ra In-ho, reporting.

519
00:31:05.406 --> 00:31:08.033
Where were you?
It's our turn to sort the recycling.

520
00:31:08.617 --> 00:31:09.451
Private Lee.

521
00:31:15.332 --> 00:31:16.333
Here.

522
00:31:17.835 --> 00:31:19.503
You didn't hand yours in earlier?

523
00:31:20.129 --> 00:31:21.380
What's wrong with you?

524
00:31:22.923 --> 00:31:24.340
Hey, it's mine.

525
00:31:24.341 --> 00:31:27.594
I told the admin supply officer
that I needed it because my kid is sick.

526
00:31:27.595 --> 00:31:28.845
Your kid is sick?

527
00:31:28.846 --> 00:31:30.513
No, sir. My son's fine.

528
00:31:30.514 --> 00:31:32.473
I got your phone instead of mine

529
00:31:32.474 --> 00:31:34.684
because it seemed like you needed it.

530
00:31:34.685 --> 00:31:36.895
What if you'd gotten caught?

531
00:31:37.354 --> 00:31:39.273
You clever devil.

532
00:31:39.815 --> 00:31:40.941
Thanks a lot.

533
00:31:41.358 --> 00:31:42.818
Ra In-ho!

534
00:31:43.777 --> 00:31:45.361
- Private Ra In-ho, reporting!
- Retreat.

535
00:31:45.362 --> 00:31:47.323
- Tap in!
- Yes, sir!

536
00:31:47.740 --> 00:31:48.740
Ra In-ho!

537
00:31:48.741 --> 00:31:50.491
Go and talk to your girlfriend.

538
00:31:50.492 --> 00:31:52.828
- I'll finish this with Private Hwang.
- Okay.

539
00:31:53.329 --> 00:31:54.246
Thanks.

540
00:31:54.622 --> 00:31:56.497
- Retreat!
- Don't let him grab you there.

541
00:31:56.498 --> 00:31:57.915
There's no way out, then.

542
00:31:57.916 --> 00:32:00.127
Is this what you want me to do?

543
00:32:00.628 --> 00:32:01.503
You punk.

544
00:32:02.087 --> 00:32:03.672
<i>Here's the next report.</i>

545
00:32:04.465 --> 00:32:08.051
<i>Today, there were more incidents in Seoul</i>

546
00:32:08.052 --> 00:32:11.180
<i>of convulsing people attacking the public.</i>

547
00:32:11.722 --> 00:32:15.516
<i>The Ministry of Health and Welfare
is monitoring the situation</i>

548
00:32:15.517 --> 00:32:17.518
<i>and has quarantined the attackers</i>

549
00:32:17.519 --> 00:32:18.978
<i>- to conduct tests.</i>
- I'm home.

550
00:32:18.979 --> 00:32:21.314
You're back at an odd hour.

551
00:32:21.315 --> 00:32:23.274
<i>In response to the potential threat
of an epidemic,</i>

552
00:32:23.275 --> 00:32:25.860
<i>- researchers were dispatched to Korea</i>
- Doesn't seem like you've been drinking.

553
00:32:25.861 --> 00:32:27.779
<i>- to conduct a joint investigation.</i>
- Of course not.

554
00:32:27.780 --> 00:32:29.490
- I was working late.
<i>- Up next...</i>

555
00:32:31.116 --> 00:32:33.994
I'm starving. Give me food.

556
00:32:35.245 --> 00:32:36.664
Did you tell Jae-yoon

557
00:32:37.623 --> 00:32:40.459
that I'll kill him
if he calls at that hour again?

558
00:32:41.585 --> 00:32:44.004
Whatever. I don't remember a thing.

559
00:32:44.630 --> 00:32:49.093
No sensible man
would call at such a late hour.

560
00:32:50.135 --> 00:32:52.137
You need to think carefully.

561
00:32:53.305 --> 00:32:55.015
If you marry someone that selfish,

562
00:32:55.724 --> 00:32:57.726
you'll suffer for the rest of your life.

563
00:32:58.727 --> 00:33:00.729
Why is everyone on about that today?

564
00:33:01.605 --> 00:33:03.439
<i>A poll was carried out</i>

565
00:33:03.440 --> 00:33:06.235
<i>among 2,509 voters over the age of 18.</i>

566
00:33:06.610 --> 00:33:09.195
<i>Compared to the previous week,
the number of people</i>

567
00:33:09.196 --> 00:33:11.615
<i>who thought positively
of the current president's--</i>

568
00:33:19.164 --> 00:33:21.166
SWEET JAE-YOON

569
00:33:22.918 --> 00:33:26.045
<i>It feels like we can never
catch each other on the phone.</i>

570
00:33:26.046 --> 00:33:27.673
Tell me about it.

571
00:33:29.383 --> 00:33:30.259
Young-joo.

572
00:33:31.051 --> 00:33:32.969
<i>I read the text you sent.</i>

573
00:33:32.970 --> 00:33:37.099
<i>I get all that about the welcome dinner
and your manager.</i>

574
00:33:37.433 --> 00:33:41.394
<i>But it's hard being cooped up here,
unable to do anything.</i>

575
00:33:41.395 --> 00:33:43.438
<i>Couldn't you be a bit more considerate?</i>

576
00:33:43.439 --> 00:33:47.192
<i>I get stressed out worrying about you.</i>

577
00:33:50.821 --> 00:33:51.822
<i>Hello?</i>

578
00:33:52.364 --> 00:33:53.741
<i>Hello? Young-joo?</i>

579
00:33:54.742 --> 00:33:55.617
<i>Hello?</i>

580
00:33:56.910 --> 00:33:58.370
- Jae-yoon.
<i>- Yes?</i>

581
00:34:01.039 --> 00:34:04.084
Why don't we take a bit of a break?

582
00:34:11.884 --> 00:34:12.801
What...

583
00:34:16.138 --> 00:34:18.599
What are you talking about?

584
00:34:21.810 --> 00:34:24.062
Are you getting back at me for nagging?

585
00:34:25.439 --> 00:34:26.315
<i>No.</i>

586
00:34:27.065 --> 00:34:29.610
<i>That's not why I'm saying this.</i>

587
00:34:30.319 --> 00:34:31.360
Why, then?

588
00:34:31.361 --> 00:34:32.988
<i>Since you got drafted,</i>

589
00:34:33.655 --> 00:34:37.201
<i>I've thought a lot about
whether or not to wait for your discharge.</i>

590
00:34:37.659 --> 00:34:40.412
<i>Let's say I manage to wait 18 months.</i>

591
00:34:41.038 --> 00:34:42.289
What's next for us?

592
00:34:45.209 --> 00:34:47.920
Where is this relationship heading?

593
00:34:51.882 --> 00:34:52.883
<i>Jae-yoon.</i>

594
00:34:53.675 --> 00:34:55.301
<i>The day you joined the army,</i>

595
00:34:55.302 --> 00:34:57.930
<i>you didn't say anything to put me at ease.</i>

596
00:34:58.305 --> 00:35:00.808
<i>And even now,
you can't answer my question.</i>

597
00:35:02.601 --> 00:35:04.352
- Private First Class Lee.
- Yes?

598
00:35:04.353 --> 00:35:06.270
Sergeant Kim asked for you.

599
00:35:06.271 --> 00:35:07.356
I'll be right there.

600
00:35:09.358 --> 00:35:10.984
- Okay.
- I'll be there soon. Go.

601
00:35:15.489 --> 00:35:16.573
<i>Jae-yoon.</i>

602
00:35:18.826 --> 00:35:20.327
<i>This isn't just hard on you.</i>

603
00:35:24.623 --> 00:35:26.166
Okay. I'll do as you say.

604
00:35:34.258 --> 00:35:35.591
- Come and eat.
- Mom!

605
00:35:35.592 --> 00:35:37.636
Will you knock first?

606
00:35:39.930 --> 00:35:41.556
What is it? Why are you crying?

607
00:35:41.557 --> 00:35:42.641
I'm not crying.

608
00:36:02.536 --> 00:36:04.620
- May I say just one thing?
- No, don't.

609
00:36:04.621 --> 00:36:06.874
Yes, sir. Copy that!

610
00:36:08.917 --> 00:36:10.294
Say it. What is it?

611
00:36:12.296 --> 00:36:14.298
Are you all right,
Private First Class Lee?

612
00:36:17.676 --> 00:36:18.969
Young-joo says

613
00:36:19.803 --> 00:36:21.263
she wants us to take a break.

614
00:36:25.976 --> 00:36:27.978
That means she wants to break up, right?

615
00:36:29.354 --> 00:36:30.898
May I say one more thing?

616
00:36:31.815 --> 00:36:34.817
When it's just us two,
you don't have to ask permission.

617
00:36:34.818 --> 00:36:37.194
You can just speak. It's fine.

618
00:36:37.195 --> 00:36:38.363
Yes, sir.

619
00:36:40.282 --> 00:36:42.159
Then, I'll ask you a question.

620
00:36:44.328 --> 00:36:47.789
Will you marry your girlfriend
once you're discharged from the army?

621
00:36:51.168 --> 00:36:52.502
Well...

622
00:36:55.172 --> 00:36:56.381
Would she marry me?

623
00:36:57.215 --> 00:36:59.468
I haven't even graduated yet.

624
00:37:01.803 --> 00:37:05.849
How long do you expect her
to wait for you?

625
00:37:08.602 --> 00:37:11.146
Waiting 18 months isn't easy.

626
00:37:11.813 --> 00:37:13.273
My wife said

627
00:37:14.441 --> 00:37:16.318
if it weren't for our son Ha-yul,

628
00:37:16.860 --> 00:37:18.737
she'd have left me long ago.

629
00:37:35.045 --> 00:37:36.922
Our cute Young-man.

630
00:37:37.589 --> 00:37:38.924
Shall I get you something?

631
00:37:39.383 --> 00:37:40.883
No need, sir.

632
00:37:40.884 --> 00:37:42.927
They said I could go down next week.

633
00:37:42.928 --> 00:37:45.012
Go and have lots of good food.

634
00:37:45.013 --> 00:37:46.013
Salute.

635
00:37:46.014 --> 00:37:47.932
There you go, sulking again.

636
00:37:47.933 --> 00:37:49.851
- I'll get you a hamburger.
- Six.

637
00:37:51.520 --> 00:37:53.020
- Take care.
- Seven.

638
00:37:53.021 --> 00:37:54.147
Bye, sir.

639
00:37:55.190 --> 00:37:56.191
Eight.

640
00:37:57.985 --> 00:37:58.944
Nine.

641
00:38:00.904 --> 00:38:01.988
Ten.

642
00:38:01.989 --> 00:38:04.408
Can you stop already? It's distracting.

643
00:38:04.741 --> 00:38:06.493
I'll do just one more set.

644
00:38:07.035 --> 00:38:10.038
Jae-yoon and In-ho fucking messed up
their reports again yesterday.

645
00:38:10.497 --> 00:38:12.331
Once I become squad commander,

646
00:38:12.332 --> 00:38:14.667
I won't let them get away with this.

647
00:38:14.668 --> 00:38:15.877
Those bastards.

648
00:38:16.586 --> 00:38:19.755
It sounds like you're saying
they get away with it

649
00:38:19.756 --> 00:38:21.591
because I'm a bad squad commander.

650
00:38:21.967 --> 00:38:25.429
Why would you take it that way, Sergeant?

651
00:38:25.721 --> 00:38:28.264
You know you're my favorite person here.

652
00:38:28.265 --> 00:38:30.099
You're my role model.

653
00:38:30.100 --> 00:38:31.351
You're all talk.

654
00:38:32.352 --> 00:38:34.730
What should we do with Jae-yoon and In-ho?

655
00:38:35.439 --> 00:38:38.316
Hell if I know.

656
00:38:38.900 --> 00:38:40.693
They're both older than us.

657
00:38:40.694 --> 00:38:42.529
Why can't they do anything right?

658
00:38:43.280 --> 00:38:46.198
If they did half as well
as our Grade-A boy here,

659
00:38:46.199 --> 00:38:47.451
I'd have no worries.

660
00:38:47.826 --> 00:38:48.826
Right, Kyung-sik?

661
00:38:48.827 --> 00:38:50.912
That's right, sir.

662
00:38:51.204 --> 00:38:52.497
What are you saying?

663
00:38:52.831 --> 00:38:54.166
Jae-yoon's your senior.

664
00:38:54.416 --> 00:38:56.333
- Kyung-sik.
- Yes, sir?

665
00:38:56.334 --> 00:38:58.962
Don't let the praise go to your head.
Respect your seniors, okay?

666
00:39:30.702 --> 00:39:33.120
Can't I get this done professionally?

667
00:39:33.121 --> 00:39:35.664
- It'll be neater and more sanitary.
- No.

668
00:39:35.665 --> 00:39:38.417
I've always wanted to shave
my boyfriend's hair before he enlisted.

669
00:39:38.418 --> 00:39:40.879
I'll make you look prettier
than the other soldiers.

670
00:39:44.466 --> 00:39:45.550
Here goes.

671
00:39:55.143 --> 00:39:56.311
Oh, no.

672
00:40:07.030 --> 00:40:07.988
Do you find this funny?

673
00:40:07.989 --> 00:40:10.659
- You look cute.
- Are you laughing?

674
00:40:11.118 --> 00:40:12.285
You're so cute.

675
00:40:14.412 --> 00:40:15.664
That's ugly. Don't do that.

676
00:40:16.748 --> 00:40:18.833
Stop it. You look ugly.

677
00:40:18.834 --> 00:40:20.585
This ugly thing's your boyfriend.

678
00:40:21.795 --> 00:40:24.214
Keep this to yourself.
Don't show it to anyone.

679
00:40:24.756 --> 00:40:25.674
Okay?

680
00:40:27.217 --> 00:40:28.093
Keep going.

681
00:40:32.347 --> 00:40:33.306
Are you crying?

682
00:40:34.975 --> 00:40:36.059
Seriously?

683
00:40:38.061 --> 00:40:39.562
I don't want to do this.

684
00:40:39.563 --> 00:40:40.480
Hey.

685
00:40:41.898 --> 00:40:44.609
You can't walk off and leave me like this!

686
00:40:44.943 --> 00:40:45.819
Hey...

687
00:40:52.993 --> 00:40:54.828
<i>Stop it. You look ugly.</i>

688
00:40:55.328 --> 00:40:56.830
<i>This ugly thing's your boyfriend.</i>

689
00:40:57.539 --> 00:40:59.456
<i>Keep this to yourself.
Don't show it to anyone.</i>

690
00:40:59.457 --> 00:41:01.084
SEO JIN-WOOK

691
00:41:03.837 --> 00:41:05.172
SEO JIN-WOOK

692
00:41:06.840 --> 00:41:08.008
Hello.

693
00:41:08.633 --> 00:41:10.260
<i>Why do you sound so down?</i>

694
00:41:11.845 --> 00:41:13.555
It's just my morning voice.

695
00:41:14.264 --> 00:41:16.265
Why are you calling on a weekend?

696
00:41:16.266 --> 00:41:20.019
<i>I've had to come uptown
to run some errands for my father,</i>

697
00:41:20.020 --> 00:41:21.771
<i>and I've just finished,</i>

698
00:41:22.230 --> 00:41:23.190
<i>but I realized</i>

699
00:41:23.857 --> 00:41:25.692
<i>your neighborhood is right nearby.</i>

700
00:41:26.401 --> 00:41:28.320
<i>So, basically right now...</i>

701
00:41:29.654 --> 00:41:31.156
<i>I'm outside your place.</i>

702
00:41:31.907 --> 00:41:32.907
What?

703
00:41:32.908 --> 00:41:34.492
You're outside my place?

704
00:41:47.631 --> 00:41:48.757
Young-joo.

705
00:41:50.258 --> 00:41:52.092
- Did I make you wait?
- No.

706
00:41:52.093 --> 00:41:53.510
I came unannounced,

707
00:41:53.511 --> 00:41:55.722
so I'm just honored
you came out to meet me.

708
00:41:56.640 --> 00:41:59.643
Let's go.
I made a reservation while I was waiting.

709
00:42:03.021 --> 00:42:05.649
I come here often
because my friend's a part owner.

710
00:42:06.775 --> 00:42:09.819
But this lunch menu
isn't as good as their dinner options.

711
00:42:10.695 --> 00:42:12.238
It's really nice here.

712
00:42:12.239 --> 00:42:14.074
The food's incredible.

713
00:42:15.575 --> 00:42:16.867
I'll order the course meal.

714
00:42:16.868 --> 00:42:18.161
Sure.

715
00:42:19.204 --> 00:42:20.454
Anyway,

716
00:42:20.455 --> 00:42:22.873
you helped a great deal
when I applied for the job.

717
00:42:22.874 --> 00:42:25.125
I get to return the favor at last.

718
00:42:25.126 --> 00:42:28.045
I'm sorry, and I'm so very grateful.

719
00:42:28.046 --> 00:42:30.172
You can return the favor another time.

720
00:42:30.173 --> 00:42:31.840
This place is expensive, so it's on me.

721
00:42:31.841 --> 00:42:34.134
No, sir. This is my treat.

722
00:42:34.135 --> 00:42:36.388
It's fine. Buy me <i>tteokbokki</i> next time.

723
00:42:36.888 --> 00:42:38.847
And we've known each other for years.

724
00:42:38.848 --> 00:42:40.224
Why do you still call me "sir"?

725
00:42:40.225 --> 00:42:41.810
When we're outside the office,

726
00:42:42.644 --> 00:42:44.019
just call me by my name.

727
00:42:44.020 --> 00:42:45.938
I can be a bit audacious.

728
00:42:45.939 --> 00:42:48.107
If I get too comfortable,
I might get too big for my britches.

729
00:42:48.108 --> 00:42:49.401
So, I can't do that.

730
00:42:49.776 --> 00:42:50.986
You're smiling at last.

731
00:42:51.444 --> 00:42:53.113
You didn't say a word in the car.

732
00:42:53.613 --> 00:42:54.906
Is something wrong?

733
00:42:55.907 --> 00:42:57.284
Is it your boyfriend?

734
00:43:00.578 --> 00:43:01.538
It is.

735
00:43:09.296 --> 00:43:11.422
MY DARLING YOUNG-JOO

736
00:43:11.423 --> 00:43:13.382
At the dinner after our department event,

737
00:43:13.383 --> 00:43:16.719
you left early and missed it,
but Jun-ho got wasted

738
00:43:16.720 --> 00:43:19.013
and kicked our dean in the stomach.

739
00:43:19.014 --> 00:43:21.516
Our dean was 60 years old then, so...

740
00:43:23.310 --> 00:43:24.769
Don't you have to take it?

741
00:43:26.521 --> 00:43:29.441
It's my boyfriend,
so the call could take a while.

742
00:43:29.816 --> 00:43:31.151
I'll call him back at home.

743
00:43:31.860 --> 00:43:32.861
Okay.

744
00:43:33.111 --> 00:43:36.656
Anyway, I never imagined
you'd take an office job.

745
00:43:37.782 --> 00:43:41.201
It's not every day that you see
such a pretty girl fix machines.

746
00:43:41.202 --> 00:43:44.622
I was the famous Goddess of Engineering.

747
00:43:46.791 --> 00:43:50.503
But my mom couldn't stand
watching me get my hands dirty.

748
00:43:51.129 --> 00:43:53.548
And I wanted an ordinary life too.

749
00:43:54.257 --> 00:43:56.885
That's why
I'm grateful for your help, sir.

750
00:43:59.095 --> 00:44:01.348
It's Seo Jin-wook. Say "Jin-wook."

751
00:44:02.599 --> 00:44:04.767
I told you I shouldn't cross that line.

752
00:44:04.768 --> 00:44:06.311
Say it. "Jin-wook."

753
00:44:06.603 --> 00:44:07.562
Sir.

754
00:44:07.896 --> 00:44:10.231
- It's not that hard.
- I can't do it.

755
00:44:20.450 --> 00:44:22.118
Hand it in for me.

756
00:44:28.166 --> 00:44:31.043
He chewed him out the whole day.

757
00:44:31.044 --> 00:44:33.713
He cursed out a kid
ten years younger than him.

758
00:44:34.214 --> 00:44:36.966
That team leader is just too crass.

759
00:44:37.550 --> 00:44:39.094
- Sir.
- Yes?

760
00:44:39.677 --> 00:44:41.012
I need to use the restroom.

761
00:44:41.304 --> 00:44:42.555
Sure. Go ahead.

762
00:44:49.270 --> 00:44:52.107
<i>You have one voicemail.</i>

763
00:44:53.817 --> 00:44:55.402
<i>Young-joo. It's me, Jae-yoon.</i>

764
00:44:57.362 --> 00:44:58.446
<i>First of all, I'm...</i>

765
00:44:59.656 --> 00:45:00.657
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

766
00:45:02.075 --> 00:45:04.202
I thought about it from your perspective.

767
00:45:07.497 --> 00:45:08.998
It really is hopeless.

768
00:45:12.252 --> 00:45:13.878
We're 26 years old,

769
00:45:15.171 --> 00:45:17.215
and we'll be 27 when I get out of here.

770
00:45:19.968 --> 00:45:23.805
I still have to graduate from university
and then find a job.

771
00:45:25.348 --> 00:45:27.058
<i>It's one thing to wait for my discharge,</i>

772
00:45:28.101 --> 00:45:30.895
<i>but I can't expect you
to wait indefinitely for me</i>

773
00:45:31.479 --> 00:45:33.022
<i>even after I leave the army.</i>

774
00:45:35.358 --> 00:45:37.068
<i>To be honest, even I'm not sure</i>

775
00:45:38.027 --> 00:45:39.362
<i>what my future will bring.</i>

776
00:45:40.905 --> 00:45:42.490
<i>So, it'd be too selfish of me.</i>

777
00:45:44.242 --> 00:45:46.953
<i>I've been trying to brush this all off</i>

778
00:45:47.537 --> 00:45:49.789
<i>with the excuse that love is enough.</i>

779
00:45:51.875 --> 00:45:53.835
<i>But I don't think that's fair.</i>

780
00:45:56.045 --> 00:45:57.130
<i>It's not fair to you.</i>

781
00:45:59.048 --> 00:46:01.217
<i>It's not fair to either of us.</i>

782
00:46:04.012 --> 00:46:05.013
<i>Young-joo.</i>

783
00:46:07.432 --> 00:46:08.600
<i>Let's break up.</i>

784
00:46:12.353 --> 00:46:14.230
<i>Thanks for everything.</i>

785
00:46:17.942 --> 00:46:19.527
<i>And I'm really sorry.</i>

786
00:46:22.405 --> 00:46:23.615
<i>Look after yourself.</i>

787
00:46:34.250 --> 00:46:35.918
<i>The phone is turned off.</i>

788
00:46:35.919 --> 00:46:38.213
<i>After the tone, please leave--</i>

789
00:46:44.344 --> 00:46:45.969
How will you get there?

790
00:46:45.970 --> 00:46:47.221
I'll take a taxi.

791
00:46:47.222 --> 00:46:49.349
See you at work on Monday.

792
00:46:53.102 --> 00:46:54.103
Young-joo.

793
00:46:59.234 --> 00:47:01.110
I'll drive you to the barracks.

794
00:47:02.946 --> 00:47:05.490
Who should I call
about the elevator, then?

795
00:47:05.782 --> 00:47:08.117
I called the machine room
because I was told to.

796
00:47:08.493 --> 00:47:09.661
I get it, okay?

797
00:47:10.078 --> 00:47:12.038
I talked to them over a week ago.

798
00:47:12.872 --> 00:47:13.748
Fine.

799
00:47:14.666 --> 00:47:17.043
They don't give a shit
because it's not their elevator.

800
00:47:21.130 --> 00:47:23.465
Do you think they can manage?

801
00:47:23.466 --> 00:47:24.508
Especially him.

802
00:47:24.509 --> 00:47:27.136
Yes, sir! I can do it, sir!

803
00:47:27.512 --> 00:47:30.138
- I have a bad feeling about this.
- Sergeants Ahn and Yoo

804
00:47:30.139 --> 00:47:31.723
will return this evening.

805
00:47:31.724 --> 00:47:33.476
Until then, the others are on duty.

806
00:47:33.893 --> 00:47:36.521
These two are the only men available
to get the gasoline.

807
00:47:40.066 --> 00:47:43.443
If something goes wrong,
it's your job to bring them in.

808
00:47:43.444 --> 00:47:44.862
Yes, sir.

809
00:47:49.576 --> 00:47:50.784
You heard him.

810
00:47:50.785 --> 00:47:52.203
Don't do anything stupid.

811
00:47:52.704 --> 00:47:55.080
Get the gasoline
from the gas station by the intersection

812
00:47:55.081 --> 00:47:57.374
and come right back here. Okay?

813
00:47:57.375 --> 00:47:59.210
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

814
00:48:11.055 --> 00:48:12.181
Private First Class Lee.

815
00:48:13.641 --> 00:48:14.767
Are you all right?

816
00:48:18.479 --> 00:48:21.816
What private wears his beret like this?

817
00:48:23.860 --> 00:48:26.112
- Hey.
- Private Ra In-ho, reporting!

818
00:48:26.654 --> 00:48:28.740
Don't go overboard. I'm fine.

819
00:48:30.575 --> 00:48:31.618
Then...

820
00:48:32.327 --> 00:48:35.079
Can we spend this on a donut?

821
00:48:36.122 --> 00:48:39.876
Something sweet to lift your spirits.

822
00:48:40.710 --> 00:48:43.004
I love the way you think.

823
00:48:43.463 --> 00:48:45.340
When did you sneak that in?

824
00:48:48.217 --> 00:48:49.635
Fine, let's get some donuts.

825
00:48:49.636 --> 00:48:51.220
Food always helps.

826
00:49:14.035 --> 00:49:16.412
We're smack in the center of Gangnam.

827
00:49:16.913 --> 00:49:19.374
- There are lots of business--
- Sirs?

828
00:49:22.543 --> 00:49:23.836
Hello, Soo-jeong.

829
00:49:24.545 --> 00:49:25.963
Yes, hello.

830
00:49:26.422 --> 00:49:29.217
- Is there a problem?
- What?

831
00:49:29.759 --> 00:49:32.886
No. I think my senior told you last time.

832
00:49:32.887 --> 00:49:35.139
Our private elevator's not working.

833
00:49:36.099 --> 00:49:37.933
I know that.

834
00:49:37.934 --> 00:49:41.270
But if you keep coming down here...

835
00:49:41.938 --> 00:49:45.524
I'm pretty sure I told your senior.

836
00:49:45.525 --> 00:49:46.943
That quack, I mean Kwak...

837
00:49:47.694 --> 00:49:48.695
Kwak Gye-young, was it?

838
00:49:49.696 --> 00:49:50.988
So, you do know his name.

839
00:49:52.990 --> 00:49:54.784
Hello, how can I help...

840
00:49:56.619 --> 00:50:00.373
The Asia Super Star Awards
starts at 4 p.m., right?

841
00:50:00.915 --> 00:50:03.835
When will the CEO
of the sponsoring company arrive?

842
00:50:04.252 --> 00:50:07.797
Why? Do you have business here too?

843
00:50:08.339 --> 00:50:10.924
I know the CEO very well.
I'd like to say hi,

844
00:50:10.925 --> 00:50:15.096
- ask about changes in the industry--
- What's up with you?

845
00:50:15.847 --> 00:50:17.139
Are you okay?

846
00:50:17.140 --> 00:50:19.433
Don't you know Alex Entertainment?

847
00:50:19.434 --> 00:50:20.392
I know them.

848
00:50:20.393 --> 00:50:21.768
I told you last time.

849
00:50:21.769 --> 00:50:23.479
- Yes, you said last time--
- Excuse me!

850
00:50:24.313 --> 00:50:26.190
You two soldiers!

851
00:50:38.202 --> 00:50:41.122
IF YOU CAN COME DOWN,
LET'S TALK FACE TO...

852
00:50:46.335 --> 00:50:48.045
I'm just asking out of curiosity.

853
00:50:49.297 --> 00:50:51.048
Are you going there

854
00:50:51.424 --> 00:50:52.508
to break up with him?

855
00:50:55.595 --> 00:50:59.140
How far out are we?

856
00:50:59.932 --> 00:51:00.933
We're almost there.

857
00:51:05.563 --> 00:51:06.522
Yes, well...

858
00:51:09.275 --> 00:51:10.193
Young-joo.

859
00:51:12.612 --> 00:51:13.863
Whatever happens,

860
00:51:14.530 --> 00:51:17.116
don't forget I'm right here
if you're ever struggling.

861
00:51:18.367 --> 00:51:21.496
As always, I'll be right next to you.

862
00:51:21.788 --> 00:51:23.122
I'll always be waiting

863
00:51:24.165 --> 00:51:25.625
like a big tree

864
00:51:26.709 --> 00:51:27.919
that you can lean on.

865
00:51:34.884 --> 00:51:36.677
Right. Sure.

866
00:51:37.303 --> 00:51:38.221
Okay.

867
00:51:57.031 --> 00:51:57.990
Why on earth

868
00:51:58.491 --> 00:52:02.285
must you do this whenever I'm on duty?

869
00:52:02.286 --> 00:52:03.204
I'm...

870
00:52:08.751 --> 00:52:10.044
Get lost.

871
00:52:15.174 --> 00:52:17.425
Private First Class Lee.
Can I say just one thing?

872
00:52:17.426 --> 00:52:18.552
What is it?

873
00:52:18.553 --> 00:52:20.095
There's no time to waste.

874
00:52:20.096 --> 00:52:22.265
- If we're unable to get the donuts--
- Hey.

875
00:52:23.558 --> 00:52:24.559
What's that?

876
00:52:28.145 --> 00:52:28.980
What is that?

877
00:52:33.901 --> 00:52:35.443
- They're coming toward us.
- I see that!

878
00:52:35.444 --> 00:52:36.486
- In-ho!
- Yes?

879
00:52:36.487 --> 00:52:38.281
- They're headed straight for us!
- Sir!

880
00:52:39.073 --> 00:52:39.907
They're coming!

